{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters","id":1260847,"title":"My problem with QC characters.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-16T00:28:22-07:00","id":1260847,"title":"My problem with QC characters.","content":"Alright my issue with QC characters is flat out they don\u2019t work like the PCs. I know if I suspend my disbelief or whatever and rearrange my sensibilities it could work out great... but I never liked extras in the other editions and while this is better I still have issues with it. Like I know the different attacks are designed to represent different story challenges while pc attacks are more simulation, like PC Jabs are weak but accurate while QC jabs are just all around crappy.<br /> <br /> Am I the only one? I\u2019ve found I have to do two sets of stats, one my house stats for QCs and two the stats I would adjust if I shared it to people who use the standard rule?<br /> <br /> Anyone else have this trouble?<br /> <br /> I know you can have a fun cinematic experience if you don\u2019t think about it, but for me it kind of breaks immersion and I have more immersion when the stats align with the PC rules. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T00:48:55-07:00","id":1260851,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I sometimes have problems with QCs but it doesn't sound the same as yours. Could you give some examples of where the rules differ, that bothers you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T01:01:21-07:00","id":1260853,"title":"","content":"Nope, don't have this problem at all. The vast majority of QCs are there to make players look and feel like amazing super-powered demigods. They accomplish that while providing a relatively minor threat. So they're working great from my perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T01:13:02-07:00","id":1260859,"title":"","content":"And example being when you look they usually have the jab attack have the same if not lesser accuracy dice then then the stronger attacks.<br /> <br /> I think though the players already seem badass, and dialing down too much makes for those unsatisfying pop culture ninja fights. Where ninjas should be tough but every dork takes the out. Or the finale of Buffy were even Anya is taking out the Ubervamps left and right. It takes you out of it sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T02:32:11-07:00","id":1260873,"title":"","content":"I don't think QC's are meant to be like extras (just here to make PCs look badass), I think it's more &quot;save the ST the time of fully statting each NPC and saving space in prep&quot;. Having tried fully statting an exalted antagonist or two...I prefer the QC format yeah.<br /> For threat level, its more a Solar thing then a QC thing (I think DBs will face harder challenges).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T03:16:59-07:00","id":1260874,"title":"","content":"Some opponents are just all around worse with their backup weapon. That\u2019s why it\u2019s worthwhile to disarm them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T03:30:03-07:00","id":1260877,"title":"","content":"Don't quite have the same issue with QC's, though I do have some. Them having a more compact presentation and just the bare bones of what you need in a fight is good. <br /> <br /> I just wish Charms which interact with stats, such as, for example, the Survival familiar buffing Charms would have interacted with the QC presentation instead of directly referencing stuff <i>which isn't detailed in your familiar's write-up</i>, forcing me to unpack the stat-block anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T03:59:45-07:00","id":1260881,"title":"","content":"My issue with QCs is mostly that they aren't that quick, especially for ones with supernatural charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T05:31:06-07:00","id":1260888,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Quick Character characters would be less of an issue for some people if they'd gone with a name that gave more emphasis to the idea of it being something stripped down to its gameplay functions rather than being easy to come up with on the fly.<br /> <br /> Certainly, I can't see an effective middle ground when it comes to custom making characters with their own supernatural powers; a lot of people at the time seemed to not find the generic spirit Charm lists very engaging, and I for one found them bland and uninteresting in every respect besides specifying a particular spirit's style or limitations*. I recall people finding the custom Charms of the Incarnate to be so good that they wanted more in that vein, but it does seem necessarily more work intensive.<br /> <br /> I think that even then, credit should be given to the likes of Adversaries and Hundred Devils, with a constant drip of fairly high quality content giving more templates to adopt.<br /> <br /> I know there are people who think the best alternative is to be given a comprehensive breakdown of how to devise and balance powers, and while I do think it will be interesting to see what Exigents get, I do feel as though a lot of what is asked for with the likes of spirits is kind of unrealistic.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Incidentally, if ever I need to cite something that Second Edition unambiguously did better than First, the mechanical write-ups for spirits would be it. Those things generally looked like an afterthought compared to the actual character bio, the Charm names were immensely generic, you got a lot of supposedly powerful spirits who barely seemed capable of anything, and they didn't even put most of the Charm write-ups in the dedicated spirit book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T10:54:32-07:00","id":1260939,"title":"","content":"Honestly I just give them attributes + abilities and run them like pc's. The written characters don't have that so its a chore to convert them; I usually don't bother and just make up my own npc's and critters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T11:14:13-07:00","id":1260949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1260877#post1260877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wish Charms which interact with stats, such as, for example, the Survival familiar buffing Charms would have interacted with the QC presentation instead of directly referencing stuff <i>which isn't detailed in your familiar's write-up</i>, forcing me to unpack the stat-block anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's significantly easier to modify the couple charms that interact with stats than to modify every QC you come across, imo. &quot;+1 to all physical ability pools&quot; wouldn't be particularly tricky to figure out as an example. Just my 2 cents, though it's been echoed by Vance.<br /> <br /> On topic, my GM prefers full character sheets to QCs, because he can make up dice pools faster, but that's just how his brain works. To me it's exactly as fast to make up a full pool size than to come up with 2 stats that make the pool. Personally I love QCs. The only beef I've had is when you have 2 different pools for say &quot;Combat movement&quot; and &quot;Flight&quot; for a bird. Like, isn't it always flying more or less? Why would those pools be different? Small inconsistencies like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T11:54:15-07:00","id":1260963,"title":"","content":"If you think a particular QC has too few dice with a particular weapon/attack, then... give them more dice with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T14:07:53-07:00","id":1260999,"title":"","content":"My issues with QC stem entirely from the places they need to interact with PC mechanics. For example, the aforementioned interaction between survival charms and QC familiar stats are pretty annoying to try and work out without an overhaul of the training charms. The other place this comes up though is with Lunar dice caps in various animal forms. (Vance confirmed my math on this in the Ask the Devs thread before he put out a moratorium on lunar dice cap questions) The QC stats include Attribute, ability AND accuracy all in the same number with no way to separate them out. This means that a lunar with an actual weapon will pretty much always have a higher dice cap than any animal form they can use simply because the accuracy from the weapon counts against the cap in the QC stats, but not in your own form.<br /> <br /> Things like this aren't exactly deal breakers for me and they can be generally houseruled away, but they're still places where the QC system falls down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T14:41:31-07:00","id":1261004,"title":"","content":"I agree, when you have some effect that needs to know a stat the QC doesn't have listed, they become more work than a full write-up would be.<br /> <br /> But, other than that, I find them fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T16:59:01-07:00","id":1261026,"title":"","content":"So, I'm just trying to make sure I know what you're saying, the stats that you come up with for your NPCs use all the base rules, because you have a difficulty with the disconnect between withering and decisive attacks? But I'm not sure how that translates into the PCs being more badass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T03:51:44-07:00","id":1261263,"title":"","content":"I have a lot of problems with QCs (both conceptually and in execution), but that they should be stronger isn't one of them. If anything, the fact that they're allowed to use their weapon accuracy for their decisive attacks makes some of the low end mortals presented feel too powerful in some situations, especially when facing pre-Exaltation PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 10-18-2018, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T07:25:43-07:00","id":1261282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261263#post1261263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a lot of problems with QCs (both conceptually and in execution), but that they should be stronger isn't one of them. If anything, the fact that they're allowed to use their weapon accuracy for their decisive attacks makes some of the low end mortals presented feel too powerful in some situations, especially when facing pre-Exaltation PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait they can use their weapon accuracy for decisive attacks?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T07:37:55-07:00","id":1261287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261263#post1261263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a lot of problems with QCs (both conceptually and in execution), but that they should be stronger isn't one of them. If anything, the fact that they're allowed to use their weapon accuracy for their decisive attacks makes some of the low end mortals presented feel too powerful in some situations, especially when facing pre-Exaltation PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? That\u2019s been the exact opposite of my experience. The grizzled, battle hardened, old veteran statline has 7 dice to attack with his main weapon, you can easily get 7 defence with only 2 dex and 2 melee. Just have a regular mundane sword and a specialty in using it, spend 4 notes on the excellency and a level 1 stunt and bam, there you go. At that point even the champion statline doesn\u2019t stand a great chance at hitting you, and with 2 in dex and melee you probably didn\u2019t design a combat focuse character.<br /> <br /> Pre-exaltation PCs though I can see having a bigger problem. I\u2019ve run a couple mortal games with 3e and I didn\u2019t really notice the issue, but my players are pretty savvy so it wouldn\u2019t be quite as apparent. At lower dice pools that extra couple of dice would make a bigger impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T07:44:57-07:00","id":1261288,"title":"","content":"Yeah that\u2019s been part of my issue when people know they aren\u2019t combat oriented yet they effortlessly take out tough guys before they even use excellencies...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T08:17:42-07:00","id":1261294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261288#post1261288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah that\u2019s been part of my issue when people know they aren\u2019t combat oriented yet they effortlessly take out tough guys before they even use excellencies...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the flip side to that if you\u2019re willing to burn three motes a turn after regen is your 13 dice, 11 decisive, of attack to his 4 parry. So you\u2019ve got one charm and 2s in your combat stats and you\u2019re pretty well safe from all but the most intensely trained and powerful mortals, and even then they\u2019ve only got a fighting chance.<br /> <br /> The thing is for the logic of the setting that makes sense, dex 2 is an average person, 2 melee represents professional soldier training, so add on solar exaltation to that and there you go. The disconnect is that those stats are REALLY trivial to just grab at chargen, so much so that even the twilight tinkerer toy maker will probably have more, even if it doesn\u2019t make a huge amount of sense. And that\u2019s before even adding charms, where somebody with melee 5 and no non-excellency charms is way worse than somebody with 12. <br /> <br /> What you\u2019re really supposed to do with those mortals and zombies and stuff is put them in a big battle group with a great commander. But for animals like the bunyip? You got me, I have no idea why they\u2019re eating up page space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T08:55:04-07:00","id":1261300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261282#post1261282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait they can use their weapon accuracy for decisive attacks?!</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always argued that NPCs are supposed to use their initiative differently to PCs. To that end gambits and low initiative decisive attacks are a useful pressure valve to prevent you from ending up with something that would play out like a slower version of 2e's rocket tag combat, it also creates more opertunities for an Exalt to get wounded or disarmed by an opponent they weren't taking seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T09:53:12-07:00","id":1261314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261300#post1261300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always argued that NPCs are supposed to use their initiative differently to PCs. To that end gambits and low initiative decisive attacks are a useful pressure valve to prevent you from ending up with something that would play out like a slower version of 2e's rocket tag combat, it also creates more opertunities for an Exalt to get wounded or disarmed by an opponent they weren't taking seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that\u2019s a good idea. It\u2019s not even like it doesn\u2019t make tactical sense, if you\u2019re outmatched you might want to first try and level the playing field, rather than bank on being able to get ahead and land a killing blow.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d combo that with some advice for how to use things like Death Moa if your players are too badass, not the Bunyip though, nothing can help that thing. Don\u2019t be afraid to give yourself stunts as often as you give them to players for similar descriptions, and be liberal with their use of willpower. I used to consider it bad form to do those things but if both me and the players aren\u2019t enjoying it otherwise then really what\u2019s the harm. It\u2019s a nice way to not fudge the rules but also maybe have a terror bird actually hit somebody with 2s in their combat ability. Maybe, if he\u2019s also got an onslaught penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T13:53:59-07:00","id":1261376,"title":"","content":"The game I'm running is martial arts themed, and I also find martial arts a very useful tool to get around not having full charmsets for all types of Exalts (Don't have Sidereal Charms? Don't have Abyssal Charms? Doesn't matter, their Martial Arts all work the same.), buuuuut one of the issues in using those with QCs is how common [Attribute] bonuses or limits are in Martial Arts Charms. Tiger is filled with [Strength]. Single-Point needs [Dex] and [Wits] for different Charms. DPC needs [Appearance]. And so on. As a result, while I use *some* QC style dice pools, I generally end up having to define multiple Attributes regardless.<br /> <br /> I also think the general guidelines for creating QCs lowball their estimates of what the average player-created character looks like, at least a little bit. The description of the 3-6 dice range is the most optimistic (and, I'd say, unrealistic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T14:25:40-07:00","id":1261384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261376#post1261376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think the general guidelines for creating QCs lowball their estimates of what the average player-created character looks like, at least a little bit. The description of the 3-6 dice range is the most optimistic (and, I'd say, unrealistic).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When the game tells you outright what skill level its dot ratings represent, and the players then proceed to ignore all of that and give their characters much higher ratings than how they would actually characterize their characters' skill levels as, <i>the game is not in the wrong</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T14:38:29-07:00","id":1261388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261384#post1261384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the game tells you outright what skill level its dot ratings represent, and the players then proceed to ignore all of that and give their characters much higher ratings than how they would actually characterize their characters' skill levels as, <i>the game is not in the wrong</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. I quibble with that. Min-maxing behavior is common enough that I'd find it naive for any game design to not anticipate it, but Exalted specifically halfway encourages it. The themes of the game play into power fantasy, and the character creation guidelines have that &quot;Yes, You Can Take A 5&quot; sidebar specifically to encourage the hesitant not to hold back.<br /> <br /> At the very least, a game about extremely extraordinary protagonists should take their extremely extraordinary nature into account.<br /> <br /> However, I will say that I suspect the poster who said that perceived power issues with QCs are largely a matter of comparing them to Solars is correct. As some have previously noted on these forums, the Solar baseline is so high that whole aspects of the system (like Onslaught Penalties) can completely cease to matter to Solars who are specced even moderately into the right area. That's not true for DBs, and may not be true for the Lunar/Sidereal tier, either (hard to say with any certainty).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T18:04:21-07:00","id":1261445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261388#post1261388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mm. I quibble with that. Min-maxing behavior is common enough that I'd find it naive for any game design to not anticipate it, but Exalted specifically halfway encourages it. The themes of the game play into power fantasy, and the character creation guidelines have that &quot;Yes, You Can Take A 5&quot; sidebar specifically to encourage the hesitant not to hold back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I don't think the problem is min-maxing so much, considering even at dex 2, melee 2 you can start to run into weird problems. I think it's more....<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261388#post1261388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least, a game about extremely extraordinary protagonists should take their extremely extraordinary nature into account.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that kinda. You can spend about 7% of your starting ability points into any skill and become the equivalent of a professional whatever. Bump that to 10% and you're an expert among experts. Anything above that basically makes you Miyamoto Musashi or Alexander the Great, perhaps even beyond that. In that aspect the book actually does exactly what it sets out to do, and then the Solar Exalted expand upon even that through excellencies, so your merely professional Solar soldier becomes Miyamoto Musashi.<br /> <br /> So even if the player isn't trying to make a combat monster, they'll still kind of breeze past half the stuff in the corebook.Which is frustrating as a ST, and even a player, because a lot of the enemies in the corebook have cool flavourful abilities that trigger on a hit, but don't actually help them hit. Or only help them hit a crashed opponent. Like boar-tusk crocodile's ability to ignore unnatural soak, also clever wording on the dev's side to make it only unnatural soak, good job there.<br /> <br /> Or the Hellboar, who's description implies that even Terrestrial Exalted are foolish to take them on. Reading that you'd think it was pretty badass. It even has two combo abilities, a Trample that automatically knocks you down if it can rush you and stomp in the same turn, and Death Stomp, that adds +5 damage to prone enemies. Dayum, that WOULD be scary. Except it's got 6 dice to that attack, so even a very combat focused mortal can bring that chance to hit down to 1% without stunts or willpower, nevermind essence.<br /> <br /> So yeah, basically it's just way too easy to chargen, or even post chargen, become way too good at too many things and one of those things might as well be combat in the dangerous world of exalted. It isn't JUST combat either, that's just a common one. That Snakefolk Merchant profile has 5 dice to his disguise check, pretty unlikely to fool anyone who didn't specifically not take awareness. But again, that's really only because you can toss 2-3 points in there, spend a mote or two of essence and become so perceptive that it might unsettle people. Like &quot;Sorry, I hate to point this out but I thought you should know, I noticed while we were talking that you floss, but you keep skipping your back molar, probably by accident.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not necessarily a bad thing, but the game should just embrace that fact and even if it assumes most exalted won't have ability scores over 2, that at least the PCs will.<br /> <br /> TLDR; It's too easy to be too good at things in comparison to the game world, even before essence is involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T22:20:14-07:00","id":1261482,"title":"","content":"To be fair, I think PCs have dice pools of 3 or 4 in quite a few areas. They're just the pools they hardly ever roll. You have enough points and freebies that you're going to end up with 5s in your character's areas of specialization unless you make a very deliberately sub-optimal choice to avoid doing so.<br /> <br /> That plus, as has already been mentioned, the game heavily encourages you to do so via various means (with Solars. Less so with other splats) that while it isn't entirely the game's fault, it is partly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-19-2018, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T23:44:56-07:00","id":1261495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261482#post1261482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, I think PCs have dice pools of 3 or 4 in quite a few areas. They're just the pools they hardly ever roll. You have enough points and freebies that you're going to end up with 5s in your character's areas of specialization unless you make a very deliberately sub-optimal choice to avoid doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I tend to find that if you pick out stuff like craft or sail or bureaucracy, stuff that's unlikely to be thrust upon you to roll to save your life and/or if somebody else in the group is already good at it you'll definitely end up with some people that have like, 2 dice, no excellency and no specialty. But there's some stuff like combat defense, awareness, resolve, that for good reason, get 2-4 points tossed in there just because they come up so commonly and not just when/where your character chooses.<br /> <br /> You also bring up a good point that I've been avoiding though, there's a lot of people who will, rightly so, just take 5 in those areas. *Sigh* One of these days I'll find a way to make a Dynastic Hellboar Safari work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T00:38:24-07:00","id":1261502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261282#post1261282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait they can use their weapon accuracy for decisive attacks?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather, they simply use the same Attack dice pool whether making decisive or withering attacks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T01:14:06-07:00","id":1261509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261388#post1261388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mm. I quibble with that. Min-maxing behavior is common enough that I'd find it naive for any game design to not anticipate it, but Exalted specifically halfway encourages it. The themes of the game play into power fantasy, and the character creation guidelines have that &quot;Yes, You Can Take A 5&quot; sidebar specifically to encourage the hesitant not to hold back.<br /> <br /> At the very least, a game about extremely extraordinary protagonists should take their extremely extraordinary nature into account.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just think it's very silly to complain that a game which is about world-shaking demigods and gives you the <i>option</i> to play a world-shaking demigod in any area of competence you wish makes characters with dot ratings that are described as extremely extraordinary... extremely extraordinary in comparison to people that are <i>not </i>world-shaking demigods.<br /> <br /> The solution to the &quot;my non-combat character with a mere 3 dots in Melee can trivially beat a veteran of multiple wars!&quot; is not to give veterans +4 dice in their relevant pools, but to refrain from making non-combat characters with a dot rating that describes an expert whose competence is above and beyond that of a well-trained professional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 10-19-2018, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T01:38:04-07:00","id":1261513,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not positive it\u2019s directly relevant but I feel it worth pointing out that, going by the general difficulty table, pretty much <i>everyone</i> in Creation is extraordinary compared to IRL. Like, that \u201cstandard professional\u201d 2+2 pool is explicitly enough to remove someone\u2019s appendix <i>on a ship in a heavy storm</i>. Similarly, Random Q.C. McSoldier\u2019s movement pool is enough to parkour in the rain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T07:43:57-07:00","id":1261557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261509#post1261509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I just think it's very silly to complain that a game which is about world-shaking demigods and gives you the <i>option</i> to play a world-shaking demigod in any area of competence you wish makes characters with dot ratings that are described as extremely extraordinary... extremely extraordinary in comparison to people that are <i>not </i>world-shaking demigods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think that the problem is that people with melee three have abilities exactly in line with what the book describes, I think actually that\u2019s a very good thing. The problem is that the game seems a bit confused about what PCs tend to actually look like mechanically. It\u2019s nearly trivial and also a very very good idea to stick 3 dots in melee, especially if you can somehow get an excellency for it. It easily lets you beat with fairly little effort and high reliability half the antagonists in the antagonist section.<br /> <br /> Which could either be solved by just cutting a bunch of the stuff out of the antagonist chapter, or even just really simplifying them down to a more compact form, basically saying \u201cyeah we know 98% of you guys are skilled beyond the ken of normal grizzled veterans, so here\u2019s some token stats in case you want to fight them anyway, but we\u2019ll save the cool abilities for more impressive foes.\u201d<br /> <br /> In a game system like Edge of Empire for Star Wars, for example, they also have some classes that are very social/lore based. Which works well with their antagonists because as a diplomat you can still contribute to fighting, but you can\u2019t just flick a few skill points into weapon training and start mowing down stormtroopers all over. In Exalted you totally can do that, and in some cases are even encouraged just to go all out. It just feels like there\u2019s a disconnect between what you can realistically expect most players to do when given that choice, and what the game presents as challenges. <br /> <br /> Essentially, why in a game about world shaking Demi-gods is the antagonist chapter full of enemies appropriate for much much lesser heroes.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not just mortals either, like Greenmaws just kind of suck, along with several others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T08:00:44-07:00","id":1261565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261445#post1261445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah, basically it's just way too easy to chargen, or even post chargen, become way too good at too many things and one of those things might as well be combat in the dangerous world of exalted. It isn't JUST combat either, that's just a common one. That Snakefolk Merchant profile has 5 dice to his disguise check, pretty unlikely to fool anyone who didn't specifically not take awareness. But again, that's really only because you can toss 2-3 points in there, spend a mote or two of essence and become so perceptive that it might unsettle people. Like &quot;Sorry, I hate to point this out but I thought you should know, I noticed while we were talking that you floss, but you keep skipping your back molar, probably by accident.&quot;<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> TLDR; It's too easy to be too good at things in comparison to the game world, even before essence is involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's very true for things that aren't combat. In my experience, optimized social characters are the hardest to fairly challenge, but I'm having strong deja vu that I've had this conversation here before and somebody popped in to tell me that I just wasn't using enough Defining Intimacies on defense or something.<br /> <br /> I will just say (and I think I've not shared this thought before) that the pass/fail binary of social rolls (and, for that matter, the Willpower expenditure to halt certain social rolls) makes playing an especially dazzling socialite less rewarding than playing someone who's extra-good at combat, or extra-good at crafting, or extra-good at sorcery. My social-heavy players have seemed somewhat discontented with being <i>as</i> good at their role as they've been. But that's drifting off-topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261513#post1261513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not positive it\u2019s directly relevant but I feel it worth pointing out that, going by the general difficulty table, pretty much <i>everyone</i> in Creation is extraordinary compared to IRL. Like, that \u201cstandard professional\u201d 2+2 pool is explicitly enough to remove someone\u2019s appendix <i>on a ship in a heavy storm</i>. Similarly, Random Q.C. McSoldier\u2019s movement pool is enough to parkour in the rain.</div> </div> </div> </div>The suggested difficulties are much worse than the suggested dice pools, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T08:10:08-07:00","id":1261566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261445#post1261445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the Hellboar, who's description implies that even Terrestrial Exalted are foolish to take them on. Reading that you'd think it was pretty badass. It even has two combo abilities, a Trample that automatically knocks you down if it can rush you and stomp in the same turn, and Death Stomp, that adds +5 damage to prone enemies. Dayum, that WOULD be scary. Except it's got 6 dice to that attack, so even a very combat focused mortal can bring that chance to hit down to 1% without stunts or willpower, nevermind essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of interpreted that as the Dragon-Blooded level equivalent of the boar that took down Robert Baratheon, pretty easily driven off but if you chase them down and don't factor the Berserker merit they could really hurt you.<br /> <br /> This is before the possibility of a pack of them, I don't know how Hellboars are supposed to work but IRL while male boars tend to be solitary female boars travel together with their collective offspring so there's the potential to ride out to deal with a single roaming monster only to find there's a whole group of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T09:56:37-07:00","id":1261596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261565#post1261565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, that's very true for things that aren't combat. In my experience, optimized social characters are the hardest to fairly challenge, but I'm having strong deja vu that I've had this conversation here before and somebody popped in to tell me that I just wasn't using enough Defining Intimacies on defense or something.<br /> <br /> I will just say (and I think I've not shared this thought before) that the pass/fail binary of social rolls (and, for that matter, the Willpower expenditure to halt certain social rolls) makes playing an especially dazzling socialite less rewarding than playing someone who's extra-good at combat, or extra-good at crafting, or extra-good at sorcery. My social-heavy players have seemed somewhat discontented with being <i>as</i> good at their role as they've been. But that's drifting off-topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that you can have some pretty good social characters, but unfortunately the player needs to really understand the somewhat complex social system really well for that to work, and be interested in more subtle gameplay in general.<br /> <br /> The social system is also more situational, you\u2019re always going to have intimacies modifying things. It\u2019s also slanted towards defence, which is a good thing, but combined with how often integrity gets favoured, most of the the social QCs aren\u2019t really equipped to do much meaningful interaction there. I feel that DBs will be slightly better for that kind of thing, since they can\u2019t so easily get a big dice cap with low ability dots, but I\u2019ll need to run a few games of them before I get a feel for it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261566#post1261566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of interpreted that as the Dragon-Blooded level equivalent of the boar that took down Robert Baratheon, pretty easily driven off but if you chase them down and don't factor the Berserker merit they could really hurt you.<br /> <br /> This is before the possibility of a pack of them, I don't know how Hellboars are supposed to work but IRL while male boars tend to be solitary female boars travel together with their collective offspring so there's the potential to ride out to deal with a single roaming monster only to find there's a whole group of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve thought of doing something like that and it could maybe work. I didn\u2019t know female boars roamed in packs so I was just going to have a big corpse attract a few, and they\u2019d be hungry enough to spend some willpower defending their kill. Maybe a dead elephant from a caravan that the PCs are investigating the disappearance of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T15:21:20-07:00","id":1261651,"title":"","content":"Perhaps it would spice things up if QC characters had abilities that trigger when they fail to do something or when they suffer an attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T21:03:58-07:00","id":1261704,"title":"","content":"QCs are literally what I have done in *every* edition of Exalted, codified. If the problem is dice... give em more. I won't tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T22:37:12-07:00","id":1261728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261565#post1261565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The suggested difficulties are much worse than the suggested dice pools, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean <i>I</i> consider it a feature. Creation is such an epic world of epic people doing epic things that it outright has a higher bar than our world for what \u201cepic\u201d <i>is</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T23:09:27-07:00","id":1261734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261728#post1261728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean <i>I</i> consider it a feature. Creation is such an epic world of epic people doing epic things that it outright has a higher bar than our world for what \u201cepic\u201d <i>is</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh... when you can potentially boost a dice pool above 20 fresh out of character creation (assuming Solar or Lunar-with-a-Stunt), &quot;near-impossible even by heroic standards&quot; topping out at Difficulty 5 feels really inadequate. It doesn't give you any conceptual framework for describing what, for instance, a 9-successes Lore roll can achieve (what's almost double a &quot;near-impossible&quot; feat?), nor does it leave much room for one.<br /> <br /> Maybe the intent really is supposed to be that you are never meant to strictly <i>need</i> more than 5 successes for any standard* roll, and the extra dice you can get are just insulation against penalties and insurance against bad rolls, but even for ludicrously epic demigods I'd like to be able to give them proportionately-ludicrous challenges other than just &quot;face opposition from someone who has equally ludicrous superpowers.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Or, alternatively,</i> there should be more applications for Threshold Successes so being better-than-you-need-to-be could be more rewarding. (I would say, for example, that Storypath's version of Stunts is a good approach to making threshold successes matter more.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*By which I mean &quot;not an opposed roll or something covered by a subsystem like Combat, Crafting, Workings, etc. that uses different guidelines for Difficulty.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-20T12:28:18-07:00","id":1261811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260847-my-problem-with-qc-characters?p=1261294#post1261294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you\u2019re really supposed to do with those mortals and zombies and stuff is put them in a big battle group with a great commander. But for animals like the bunyip? You got me, I have no idea why they\u2019re eating up page space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Animals perform their best when they're essentially exotic pets. For example a female Bunyip can give you a free Defend Other with Parry 5 if you're willing to abide the ridiculousness of riding around like a baby marsupial because you're also mounted so +1 defence there.<br /> I'm imagining a diminutive assassin emerging from the pouch and firing poisoned blow darts at people because that should be pretty memorable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}